<p>File access lives on <code>Io</code>. Every call can fail with <code>IoError</code> (<code>notFound</code>, <code>permissionDenied</code>, <code>invalidUtf8</code>, <code>notADirectory</code>, <code>other</code>, <code>invalidInput</code>, <code>unsupported</code>); none throws. Catch it, or pass it on with <code>try</code> from a function declaring <code>fails IoError</code>. Public file functions also declare <code>uses fs</code> (<a href="cookbook-errors.html#effects">Errors</a>).</p>
<p>Examples write under <code>/tmp</code> to run on macOS and Linux.</p>

<h2 id="read-file">Read a whole file</h2>
<p><code>Io.readText(path)</code> returns a <code>string</code>, failing <code>invalidUtf8</code> on bytes that are not valid text. <code>Io.readFile(path)</code> returns a <code>List&lt;u8&gt;</code> with no decoding.</p>
<example name="cookbook-read-file"/>
<pre><code class="other" data-lang="Python">text = open(path).read()   # raises FileNotFoundError</code></pre>

<h2 id="read-lines">Read a file line by line</h2>
<p>Read the text, then walk <code>text.lines</code>, a lazy view splitting on <code>\n</code> or <code>\r\n</code> without copying (as above). <strong>Not in the standard library yet:</strong> a streaming reader holding one line; <code>Io.readText</code> loads the whole file.</p>

<h2 id="write-file">Write or append to a file</h2>
<p><code>Io.writeFile(path, bytes)</code> takes bytes, replaces the content and returns nothing. Pass <code>text.bytes</code> for text, a span for binary data. It creates no missing directories. <strong>Not in the standard library yet:</strong> append and directory creation; to append, read the file, build the longer text and write it back (below).</p>
<example name="cookbook-write-file"/>

<h2 id="paths">Join and take apart file paths</h2>
<p><strong>Planned: joining.</strong> The spec defines <code>Path.join</code> with variable segments (§10) and a <code>Path</code> type in signatures (<code>copy(from Path src, to Path dst)</code>). The compiler has no <code>Path</code> yet; a path is a plain <code>string</code>, built with interpolation (<code>$"{dir}/{name}.txt"</code>).</p>
<pre><code class="byn">let p = Path.join(root, "orders", $"{id}.json")</code></pre>
<p><strong>Not in the standard library yet:</strong> base name, directory name and extension; the spec defines none.</p>
<pre><code class="other" data-lang="Go">filepath.Join(root, "orders", id+".json")
filepath.Base(p); filepath.Dir(p); filepath.Ext(p)</code></pre>

<h2 id="list-dir">List a directory</h2>
<p><code>Io.listDir(path)</code> returns entry names in byte order, without the directory prefix. A file gives <code>notADirectory</code>; a missing path, <code>notFound</code>. <strong>Not in the standard library yet:</strong> walking a directory tree, and telling files from directories in a listing; <code>listDir</code> returns names only.</p>
